# Secrets never enter an image. `COPY . .` would otherwise bake .env into a
# layer, where it survives every later deletion and travels with the image to
# wherever it is pushed. Configuration reaches the container through the
# environment instead; Config.load() prefers a real environment variable over
# anything it reads from a file, so this is not a limitation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output and state, not source. The vector index is a volume.
node_modules
data
*.log

# Not needed at runtime, and large.
.git
.github
tests
coverage
.vscode
.idea

# templates/ and its site.css are the pages themselves — every HTML response is
# assembled from them at runtime. Excluding them would build an image that
# starts, answers /health, and 500s on every page a person can see.

# docs/ IS needed at runtime: /about, /terms and /about/crawler are rendered
# from the Markdown in it, so that the terms on the site and the terms in the
# repository cannot drift. Excluding it built an image that served 500s on
# those three routes and nothing else. 204K of text is not worth the saving.
